LICENSING OF THE FILES IN THIS FOLDER
=====================================

There are two kinds of file here, and they are not under the same terms.

1. ChromIQ's own files
----------------------
README.md, this file, and `fogra/SOURCE.json` are ChromIQ's own work and are
covered by the project's licence, the GNU Affero General Public License version
3, the same as the rest of ChromIQ. A copy is in the LICENSE file at the root of
the project.

`fogra/SOURCE.json` contains no colour data. It records where each data file
came from, under what terms, and its sha256 as shipped.

2. Third-party reference data
-----------------------------
Everything in `fogra/` except `SOURCE.json` is Fogra's, not ChromIQ's, and is
governed by the terms Fogra states, not by the licence above. ChromIQ may not
relicense it.

  Fogra          Free use and redistribution of the Fogra characterisation
  Forschungs-    data is permitted, including redistribution as part of
  institut für   commercial and non-commercial software, provided that the
  Medien-        data are distributed unmodified and Fogra is identified as
  technologien   the source. The designation FOGRAxx may be used solely to
  e.V.           identify the respective reference data. Such use does not
                 imply certification, approval or endorsement by Fogra.

                 Quoted from
                 https://fogra.org/en/downloads/work-tools/characterisation-data
                 as read on 2026-09-10, and matching the grant given in
                 writing by Dr.-Ing. Andreas Kraushaar and recorded in
                 docs/design/issue_182_answers.md.

The files are Fogra's own bytes from
`MK3_Subsets_FOGRA39_until_FOGRA60.zip` (V1.0, published 2022-01-27),
downloaded 2026-09-10. Their sha256 sums are in `fogra/SOURCE.json` so that
"distributed unmodified" can be checked rather than asserted, and
`tests/test_reference_sets.py` checks it.

Nothing in this folder is ISO's. No tolerance value of any ISO standard is here,
in any file ChromIQ ships, or on any branch it is released from. Characterisation
data and tolerance values are different things with different owners, and only
the Fogra half is cleared.

Anyone adding a file to this folder has to add its source and its terms to
`fogra/SOURCE.json` in the same change. The loader refuses a file that has no
entry, so a data file physically cannot be offered without its credit.
